Subject: [PATCH 5/5] D15: privacy is an optional feature, integrated not
 rebuilt; CreateX preinstalled
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Two decisions taken 2026-09-28.

D15(a): privacy is an OPTIONAL feature, not a defining property. The public path
stays first-class (threat-model P6) — Konstellation is a chain that offers
privacy, not a privacy chain. That is the reading consistent with D6's chain-wide
compliance and D7's permissioned launch, and it keeps D14's accepted leak
defensible in public rather than in tension with the marketing.

D15(b): integrate 0xbow-io/privacy-pools-core (Apache-2.0, four audits), proven
working end to end on Konstellation by the P0-A spike. Building our own ZK
protocol is explicitly out — strategy §13 ranks custom cryptography a
catastrophic-failure risk and Appendix A says prefer upstream reuse.

Sequencing is deliberately NOT settled by D15: testnet-1 first, mainnet only once
baseline activity gives a real anonymity set. §18 carries the row, since this is
a testnet-first difference. A pool launched into thin volume gives its first users
a guarantee that is sound in form and absent in practice.

Still open before mainnet: who holds the association-set key (§10), and whether
Cosmos's native ZK-UTXO module (H1 2026, alongside x/poa) supersedes the
application-layer path.

CreateX is now in the genesis preinstall set, taking it to 11. Pinned in contracts
from three independent mainnet RPCs with the codeHash matching mainnet's own
eth_getProof, wired in konstellation/app/preinstalls, and verified on a fresh
chain — 11,838 bytes on chain and deployCreate() deploys successfully. It is
AGPL-3.0-only, unlike the rest of the set, which wants an explicit human decision
before mainnet genesis.

